\frac{3x+5x}{2}+4y & = \\\\ \\frac{8x}{2}+4y & = \\\\ 4\\,x+4\\,y\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459293 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459158 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459293 #edb/ref 1069 "q-100054" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459293 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459293 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the expression $\\frac{6x}{5}+15-\\frac{4x}{7}+8.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459293 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dc80fc0c-88ad-5f7a-b174-a89a65c11a38" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459293 #edb/ref 1074 "We collect and combine the like terms, simplifying the coefficients as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6x}{5}+15-\\frac{4x}{7}+8 & = \\\\ (\\frac{6x}{5}-\\frac{4x}{7})+(15+8) & = \\\\ (\\frac{42x}{35}-\\frac{20x}{35})+(15+8) & = \\\\ (\\frac{42x-20x}{35})+23 & = \\\\ \\frac{22x}{35}+23\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
